title: Commvault VM Backup
agents: commvault_rest
catalog: app/other
license: GPLv2
distribution:
description:
 Piggyback check on the VM host: SLA status (met OK, missed CRIT, excluded
 OK), protection status (PROTECTED OK, WARNING WARN, FAILED CRIT,
 NOT_PROTECTED WARN, DISCOVERED WARN), last backup with failure reason and the
 age of the last successful backup (optional levels). VMs excluded from the
 SLA are not evaluated further. All states are configurable in the ruleset
 "Commvault VM backup".

 The piggyback host name is the VM name (characters other than letters,
 digits, dot, dash and underscore replaced by "_"). If several Commvault
 entries share a name, the entry with SLA and the most recent backup wins;
 the others are listed in the details.

discovery:
 One service on every piggyback host (VM) delivered by the special agent.
